/	MEMORY SIZING PROGRAM.

/	THIS PROGRAM DETERMINES THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD ON ANY PDP-8 MODEL IN THE
/	"FAMILY OF 8" OR DECMATE.  NOTE: PROPER EXECUTION IS NOT GUARANTEED WHEN
/	ATTEMPTED ON THE PDP-5 OR PDP-8/S.  THE PROGRAM IS WRITTEN FOR USE EITHER
/	STANDALONE OR FOR USE WITH OPERATING SYSTEMS SUCH AS P?S/8 AND OS/8 WHERE THE
/	ACTUAL MEMORY AVAILABLE COULD EXCEED THE MINIMUM SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS.  NOTE:
/	THE PROGRAM REQUIRES THE PRESENCE OF FIELD 0; OS/8 ALSO REQUIRES FIELD 1 AND
/	IN CERTAIN CONFIGURATIONS FIELD 2.  CERTAIN CONFIGURATIONS OF P?S/8 REQUIRE
/	AT LEAST 8K MEMORY WHILE MOST CAN RUN IN 4K.

/	SINCE THE ENVIRONMENT THIS PROGRAM WILL BE USED IN IS NOT KNOWN, THE PRIOR
/	CONTENTS OF TEST LOCATIONS WILL BE SAVED BEFORE TESTING AND RESTORED
/	AFTERWARDS.

/	SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS.

/	1) CERTAIN MODELS OF PDP-8/I, PDP-8/L AND PDP-12 HAVE SPECIFIC QUIRKS
/	   REGARDING THE VALUE RETURNED WHEN ACCESSING NONEXISTENT MEMORY FIELDS THAT
/	   DEPEND ON THE EXACT CONFIGURATION.  THE VALUES RETURNED ARE EITHER 0000 OR
/	   7777; AS SUCH, THIS PROGRAM WILL USE OTHER TEST VALUES TO AVOID CONFUSED
/	   DETECTION RESULTS.

/	2) ORIGINAL PDP-8 AND LINC-8 SYSTEMS WITH EXTENDED MEMORY HAVE A PARTICULARLY
/	   UNUSUAL QUIRK WHEN WRITING TO NONEXISTENT MEMORY.  THE INSTRUCTION TO
/	   STORE INTO MEMORY IS INHIBITED; INSTEAD, THE DATA IN THE ACCUMULATOR IS
/	   EXECUTED AS IF AN INSTRUCTION IN MEMORY.  IT IS NOT CERTAIN IF THE
/	   ACCUMULATOR CONTENTS ARE ALTERED IN THIS SITUATION.  AS SUCH, THE PROGRAM
/	   USES THE VALUE 7000 [NOP] AS THE TEST VALUE TO BE STORED.  EXECUTION
/	   CONTINUES AFTER THE ORIGINAL INSTRUCTION LOCATION ATTEMPT, LIKELY SKIPPING
/	   TO THE NEXT LOCATION AFTERWARDS.  AS SUCH, THE PROGRAM LOGIC WILL DETERMINE
/	   THE ATTEMPT WAS NOT SUCCESSFUL; NO ATTEMPT WILL BE MADE TO RESTORE THE
/	   SUPPOSED FORMER CONTENTS IN THIS SITUATION.

/	3) IN THE SPECIFIC CASE OF THE PDP-8/L, CDF INSTRUCTIONS TO NONEXISTENT FIELDS
/	   ARE INHIBITED; THE PREVIOUS DATA FIELD STILL APPLIES.  AS SUCH, THE PROGRAM
/	   ALWAYS RESETS THE DATA FIELD TO 00 AND THE PROGRAM CHECKS IF THE
/	   CORRESPONDING LOCATION IN FIELD 0 IS MODIFIED [AND BECOMES THE TEST VALUE
/	   INSTEAD OF THE FORMER VALUE].  IF ANY TEST ATTEMPT STORES THE TEST VALUE
/	   INTO THE CORRESPONDING FIELD 0 LOCATION, THE ATTEMPT CLEARLY FAILED; THE
/	   MEMORY IS THE SIZE OF ALL PRIOR FIELDS THAT PASSED TESTING.

/	PROGRAM DEFINITIONS.

	SBOOT=	7600			/EXIT LOCATION FOR MOST OPERATING SYSTEMS.
	TESTLOC=0020			/TEST LOCATION.
/	THE PROGRAM STARTS HERE.

	FIELD	0			/MUST BE LOADED IN FIELD 0.

	*200				/THE USUAL STARTING LOCATION.

	NOP				/IN CASE THIS PROGRAM IS CHAINED TO.
	CLA CLL				/CLEAN UP.

/	THE CONSOLE OUTPUT FLAG MAY ALREADY BE UP.

	TSF				/FLAG ALREADY UP [P?S/8 STYLE]?
	TLS				/NO, RAISE IT NOW TO PRIME THE PUMP.

/	AT THIS POINT THE OUTPUT FLAG IS EITHER UP NOW OR WILL BE SHORTLY.

	DCA	TESTLOC			/CLEAR FAILING TEST LOCATION.
	TAD	(-7)			/SETUP THE
	DCA	TESTCNT			/TEST COUNTER.
	TAD	(CDF	10)		/GET INITIAL TEST VALUE.
	DCA	TESTCDF			/STORE INLINE.

TRYNEXT,CDF	00			/RESET TO FIELD 0 IN CASE PDP-8/L.
TESTCDF,.-.				/WILL BE "CDF XX" WHERE XX IS LATEST TEST FIELD.
	TAD I	(TESTLOC)		/GET THE CURRENT CONTENTS [IF POSSIBLE].
	DCA	CONTEMP			/STORE IT FOR LATER.
	TAD	(NOP)			/GET THE TEST VALUE.
	DCA I	(TESTLOC)		/STORE IT [HOPEFULLY].
	TAD I	(TESTLOC)		/GET IT BACK [HOPEFULLY].
	TAD	(-NOP)			/COMPARE TO EXPECTED VALUE.
	SNA				/SKIP IF ALREADY DIFFERENT FROM EXPECTED.
	TAD	TESTLOC			/ELSE COMPARE TO POTENTIALLY CHANGED LOCATION.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF THIS TEST SUCCEEDED.
	JMP	TESTEND			/JUMP IF NOT.

/	THIS TEST SUCCEEDED; RESTORE THE FORMER CONTENTS AND SETUP NEXT.

	TAD	CONTEMP			/GET THE OLD VALUE.
	DCA I	(TESTLOC)		/RESTORE IT.
	TAD	TESTCDF			/GET LATEST TEST CDF INSTRUCTION.
	TAD	(10)			/BUMP TO NEXT TEST FIELD.
	DCA	TESTCDF			/STORE BACK.
	ISZ	TESTCNT			/CHECKED ALL POTENTIAL FIELDS?
	JMP	TRYNEXT			/NO, GO BACK AND DO ANOTHER ONE.

/	COMES HERE WHEN NO FURTHER TESTING IS POSSIBLE [OR NEEDED].

TESTEND,CDF	00			/MAKE SURE FIELD 0.

/	THE TEST COUNTER CONTAINS THE TOTAL AVAILABLE MEMORY FIELD COUNT.  CONVERT THE
/	VALUE INTO AN ASCII TEXT CHARACTER.

	TAD	TESTCNT			/GET THE COUNTER
	TAD	("0+7)			/CONVERT TO A CHARACTER BETWEEN "0" AND "7".
	DCA	FLDCHAR			/STORE IN THE MESSAGE TEXT.
PLOOP,	TAD I	TXTPTR			/GET A CHARACTER IN THE MESSAGE.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT AT THE END OF THE MESSAGE.
	JMP I	(SBOOT)			/EXIT; CHANGE TO 7402 [HLT] IF STANDALONE.
	TSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	TLS				/YES, OUTPUT IT NOW.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP
	ISZ	TXTPTR			/BUMP TO NEXT CHARACTER IN THE STRING.
	JMP	PLOOP			/KEEP GOING.

CONTEMP,.-.				/TEMPORARY STORAGE FOR ORIGINAL CONTENTS.
TESTCNT,.-.				/MEMORY FIELD TEST COUNTER.
TXTPTR,	MSTRNG				/TEXT POINTER [ALREADY INITIALIZED].
MSTRNG,	"T;"H;"E;" ;"H;"I;"G;"H;"E;"S;"T
	" ;"A;"V;"A;"I;"L;"A;"B;"L;"E;" 
	"M;"E;"M;"O;"R;"Y;" ;"F;"I;"E;"L;"D
	" ;"I;"S;" 
FLDCHAR,.-.				/THIS WILL BE THE HIGHEST FIELD [CHARACTER].
	"M&37;"J&37;0			/<CR> THEN <LF> ENDS THE PRINTED MESSAGE.

	$				/THAT'S ALL FOLK!

/	COMMENT RULER FOR SUCH AS THIS.  FOR NON-COMMENT STATEMENTS, TWO MORE ALLOWED.

/	123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678